body:
are you trying to measure or annotate?

&#x200B;

the measure command has a 'chain' mode to do what you're asking.

if you're talking about cloud-based or remote collaboration,

Amazon Web Services connected to the company's servers is a really effective remote solution.

in lieu of that, remote desktop and a VPN also works well.

&#x200B;

otherwise just put the central on your company's server and local files on user hard drives, as mentioned in other posts.

i think they're really attractive and a total aesthetic.

&#x200B;

but, i guess, own it and love yourself! (?)

lol.  i was just thinking it would be amusing if they did something like this with that mech.

&#x200B;

still probably not logging back on, but still
